.th PCAT I 12/12/75
.sh NAME
pcat  \*-  expand compressed file to standard output
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd pcat
filename ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
Concatenates packed files as cat does unpacked files. Thus, to
make a usable copy, c, of a packed file, x.z, without destroying
x.z, use the command
.ti 5
pcat x > c
.br
To view a packed file x.z use the command
.ti 5
pcat x
.br
.sh "SEE ALSO"
PACK(I), UNPACK(I)
.sh AUTHOR
Steve Zucker
